    "https://www.stmarytx.edu/academics/career-center/": {
      "title": "Career and Professional Development Center",
      "description": "Career and Professional Development Center | St. Mary's University | San Antonio, TX St. Mary's University 1 Camino Santa Maria San Antonio , TX 78228 +1-210-436-3011 https://www.stmarytx.edu William Joseph Chaminade Skip to main content Resources For: Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parent & Family Apply Visit Request Info Give Now About Events Calendar History Leadership Map Mission Rankings Academics Career Center Centers and Institutes Degrees and Programs Faculty Registrar Research Schools Student Success Admission Apply for Admission Cost and Aid Graduate Military Orientation Tuition and Fees Visit Campus Athletics Campus Life Student Housing and Amenities Spiritual Life Student Life Student Services Center for International Programs Outreach Camps Counseling Service STEM Outreach  Search  Submit Rattler Careers Website Contact Us ▼ Career and Professional Development Center The Career and Professional Development Center is committed to helping you find a vocation that aligns with your personal values and educational background. At St. Mary's, we prepare you for more than just a career; we prepare you for your life's work that is your true calling. Rattler Careers Website Contact Us ▼ Home » Academics » Career and Professional Development Center Rattler Careers The Career and Professional Development Center offers online resources to students, alumni and employers. Explore industry insights, find jobs and internships, and more. To get started, select your status below. Students Kickstart your career The St. Mary’s University Career and Professional Development Center has a wide range of services to support you along your career journey. Student Alumni a Career full of Success Rattler alumni have full access to the resources and career coaching services available. Continue along the path of a successful career. Alumni Employers Become an Employer Partner Our Employer Partner Program offers a tailored strategy to help achieve your organization’s goals. We look forward to collaborating with you. Employer Colleges of Distinction St. Mary’s University has been recognized as one of the 2026-2027 Colleges of Distinction for Career Development. Learn more about St. Mary’s Honors and Rankings . A Career Full of Purpose The Career and Professional Development Center uses the Define, Discover, Do model. This model allows our Career Coaches to meet each student wherever they are on their career journey. They are here to help you along each step. Schedule an appointment to learn more about specific career options and resources at St. Mary’s. Define Define what direction you want to pursue by exploring your interests. Discover Discover which majors, skills, careers and education requirements are in demand based on your interests. Do Time to take action. Apply your knowledge through internships, career events and professional organizations. Schedule Appointment “As part of our Catholic and Marianist mission, St. Mary’s University is dedicated to helping students discover their purpose and vocation.” Stephanie Ward, Ph.D. Vice Provost for Student Success and Vocation Looking for a Job? Build your resume Expand your network Review industry and salary trends Build Skills Create resume Find jobs and internships Prepare for interviews View more resources to help you on your career journey or schedule a meeting with a St. Mary’s career coach . View Resources Career Fairs and Events The Career and Professional Development Center makes facilities and services available to St. Mary’s students and alumni looking to obtain a job or network with employers. Employing organizations with full or part-time jobs and internships can also apply to these events to connect with our community. View Fairs and Events Visit Us The Career and Professional Development Center St. Mary’s University University Center, First Floor Office Hours Monday through Friday 8 a.m. to 5 p.m. Contact Us Phone: 210-436-3102 Fax: 210-431-2231 Email: rattlercareers@stmarytx.edu Connect with Us Facebook Twitter Instagram LinkedIn @StMUCareer Back to top Request Info Visit Apply Compliance Directory Gateway HR Jobs Police Policies Privacy Reporting Webmail St. Mary’s University Websites Campus Map Nondiscrimination / Title IX Do Not Sell or Share My Personal Information List of social media accounts © 2026 All rights reserved. Contact 210-436-3011 One Camino Santa Maria, San Antonio, TX 78228. We use cookies to collect and analyze information on site performance and usage, and to enhance and customize content and targeted advertisements. Accept Cookies Reject Cookies Cookie Policy You can revoke your consent any time using the Cookie Notice button. Cookie Notice"
    },
    "https://www.stmarytx.edu/academics/faculty/": {
      "title": "Faculty",
      "description": "Faculty - St. Mary's University St. Mary's University 1 Camino Santa Maria San Antonio , TX 78228 +1-210-436-3011 https://www.stmarytx.edu William Joseph Chaminade Skip to main content Resources For: Students Alumni Faculty & Staff Parent & Family Apply Visit Request Info Give Now About Events Calendar History Leadership Map Mission Rankings Academics Career Center Centers and Institutes Degrees and Programs Faculty Registrar Research Schools Student Success Admission Apply for Admission Cost and Aid Graduate Military Orientation Tuition and Fees Visit Campus Athletics Campus Life Student Housing and Amenities Spiritual Life Student Life Student Services Center for International Programs Outreach Camps Counseling Service STEM Outreach  Search  Submit Faculty Home » Academics » Faculty With a student-to-faculty ratio of 11:1, St. Mary's faculty work closely with students to help them develop a plan for success not only in academics but in their lives. Browse faculty profiles below to learn more about their educational background and personal interests, or see the employee directory to find individual offices and campus mailboxes. St. Mary's University Faculty The profiles below include faculty in the Greehey School of Business, College of Arts, Humanities and Social Sciences, and School of Science, Engineering and Technology. School of Law faculty can be found on the School of Law website . Faculty Ben Abbott, Ph.D. Lecturer of Engineering Pius Adelani, Ph.D. Associate Professor of Chemistry Sharmin Aktar, Ph.D. Assistant Professor of Computer Science Ozgur Aktunc, Ph.D. Professor of Software Engineering Mark Alexander, D.M.A. Adjunct Professor of Piano Mehran Aminian, Ph.D. Professor of Electrical Engineering George Anquandah, Ph.D. Senior Lecturer of Chemistry and Biochemistry Mauricio Aristizabal, Ph.D. Assistant Professor of Mechanical Engineering Janet Armitage, Ph.D., MBA Chair of Sociology Leah Arreguin, Ph.D Visiting Assistant Professo